# MPC-MZ final runs (V-res-5: the shared lambda selection of mpc_lambda.fit_lambda, 1601 nodes). jobq2
# format; DO NOT START until the coordinator says so. Reads the final p6 T31_mz_rules_* / mz_tuned_* files.
#   cd <tree> && nohup python3 -I jobq2.py jobs/mz_final.jsonl > logs_jobq2_mz.txt 2>&1 &
# Cost (measured on this box under load ~3.5 on 2 cores; unloaded ~0.6x): one tuning-window MPC-24 at 1601
# nodes costs about a + b L seconds for a batch of L lambdas, 1x1: a = 21, b = 14.5; 2x2 (4 rooms): x3.3
# (1x4 the same; 1x2 ~x2). A fit is typically 3 batches per window (25-value scan + 2 x 8 refinement) on 6
# tuning windows plus 7 held-out runs (more if bisection or the §16 back-off knob is needed):
#   1x1 ~70 min, 1x2 ~2.3 h, 2x2 / 1x4 ~3.8 h (loaded; up to ~2x with bisection / back-off).
# jobq2 hard-kills at 2 h, so every cell is a CHAIN of budgeted jobs: `--budget-min 80` stops (rc 0) before
# starting a new window batch after 80 min (one 2x2 batch <= ~21 min, so every job ends < ~105 min),
# saving every computed row in results/mz_cache/<name>.pkl (keyed by the run and the code sha); the next
# job replays the deterministic selection from the cache and continues. Non-final jobs declare the chain
# marker results/mz_cache/<name>.progress; the last job (--final) must finish and declares the CSVs
# (a chain that runs out is a visible FAIL, never a silent partial table). Chain lengths: 1x1 2, 1x2 3,
# 2x2 / 1x4 5 jobs (a chain that finishes early: the remaining jobs replay from the cache in seconds).
